.\" Manpage for todo
.TH TODO 1 "2025-06-04" "v2.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
todo \- Command-line To-Do List Manager

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B todo
\[ 
.I COMMAND 
\] \[ 
.I OPTIONS 
\] \[ 
.I ARGUMENTS 
\]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B todo
is a Python-based CLI application for managing hierarchical to-do lists, subtasks, priorities, tags, categories, notes, and more.  Data is stored in \$HOME/.todo\_data.json for persistent, private usage.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new
Add a new primary task.
.TP
.B subtask
Add a subtask under a primary task.
.TP
.B pending
Mark a task or subtask as “in-progress.”
.TP
.B hold
Mark a task or subtask as “on-hold.”
.TP
.B complete
Mark one or more tasks/subtasks as complete.
.TP
.B delete
Delete one or more tasks/subtasks.
.TP
.B edit
Edit (overwrite) fields on a task or subtask.
.TP
.B update
Append to fields (notes, tags, categories, priority, description) on a task or subtask.
.TP
.B append
Append freeform text to a task or subtask’s description or notes.
.TP
.B list
List tasks and subtasks, with options for filtering, sorting, and display customization.
.TP
.B calendar
Show a colored calendar view of due tasks (current month by default).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help message.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-due " \[DATE]"
Set or filter by due date (YYYY-MM-DD, or natural language like “tomorrow,” “1 week,” etc.).
.TP
.BR \-\-AssignedTo " \[NAME]"
Assign the task or subtask to a user.
.TP
.BR \-\-priority " \[critical|high|medium|low]"
Set or update priority level (colorized in output).
.TP
.BR \-\-notes " \[TEXT]"
Attach or append notes to a task or subtask.
.TP
.BR \-\-tags " \[TAG1 TAG2 ...]"
Attach or append tags for filtering or categorization.
.TP
.BR \-\-categories " \[CAT1 CAT2 ...]"
Attach or append categories for filtering or organization.
.TP
.BR \-\-all
Show all tasks (including completed) when listing.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort " \[id|due|assigned|priority]"
Sort tasks in listings.
.TP
.BR \-\-due-today
Filter list to tasks due today.
.TP
.BR \-\-due-tomorrow
Filter list to tasks due tomorrow.
.TP
.BR \-\-due-this-month
Filter list to tasks due in the current month.
.TP
.BR \-\-due-year " \[YYYY]      \-\-due-month "\[MM]"
Filter list to tasks due in a specific year and month.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show help message for any command.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add a primary task:
.B todo new "Write report" \-\-due 2025-06-10 \-\-AssignedTo Alice \-\-priority high \-\-notes "Include exec summary" \-\-tags work urgent \-\-categories business
.TP
Add a subtask:
.B todo subtask 1 "Draft outline" \-\-due 2025-06-12 \-\-notes "Use Q2 template" \-\-tags outline
.TP
List all tasks, sorted by due date:
.B todo list \-\-sort due
.TP
List tasks with a specific tag:
.B todo list \-\-tags urgent
.TP
Mark a subtask as in-progress:
.B todo pending 1-2
.TP
Complete multiple tasks/subtasks:
.B todo complete 1-1 2 3
.TP
Delete multiple tasks or subtasks:
.B todo delete 4 5-2
.TP
Edit (overwrite) a task’s description and due date:
.B todo edit 3 \-\-description "Update requirements" \-\-due 2025-07-01
.TP
Append a note and tag to a task:
.B todo update 3 \-\-notes "Follow-up needed" \-\-tags followup
.TP
Append freeform text to a subtask’s description:
.B todo append 2-1 \-\-AD "additional context here"
.TP
Show a calendar of due tasks for June 2025:
.B todo calendar 2025 06

.SH FILES
.TP
.I \$HOME/.todo\_data.json
The JSON data file used for storing tasks.

